{"id": "q001", "question": "why doesn't the personal os just keep all my data in its own database?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}], "answer": "Based on the search results, the answer to the question \"why doesn't the personal os just keep all my data in its own database?\" is:\n\nThe Personal OS is designed to be a unified control layer over existing digital tools, not a replacement for them. Each service should remain the source of truth for the information it owns, and the Personal OS should provide unified navigation, search, and context across services.", "sources": [{"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "ADR-002-postgres-over-sqlite", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-002-postgres-over-sqlite.md"}, {"title": "ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store.md"}, {"title": "ADR-004-entity-map-from-day-one", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-004-entity-map-from-day-one.md"}, {"title": "ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1274, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 22.6, "load_seconds": 6.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 4714, "output_tokens": 83, "seconds": 96.4, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 435.7, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q002", "question": "why obsidian and not notion for storing notes?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store.md"}], "answer": "The reason for choosing Obsidian over Notion for storing notes is that Obsidian uses a lock-in-prone format and has no API, making it the least lock-in-prone format available. Additionally, using Notion would have added API auth to the very first integration, and Notion's block model is a much heavier thing to parse than frontmatter and wikilinks.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "ADR-005-obsidian-read-only-v1", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-005-obsidian-read-only-v1.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}, {"title": "ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1684, "output_tokens": 14, "seconds": 30.3, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 2238, "output_tokens": 77, "seconds": 48.6, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 5852.8, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q003", "question": "why did we skip an ORM, wouldn't it make switching databases easier?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "similar-docs"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-003-raw-sql-over-orm.md"}], "answer": "We skipped an ORM because we have a deliberate choice of Postgres, and the schema is small and mostly append-only, making manual SQL and versioned `.sql` files a suitable choice.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-003-raw-sql-over-orm", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-003-raw-sql-over-orm.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}, {"title": "ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 2025, "output_tokens": 15, "seconds": 37.1, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 2646, "output_tokens": 39, "seconds": 54.6, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 1702.2, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q004", "question": "why do we write the Google and GitHub connections ourselves instead of using existing MCP servers?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-006-direct-apis-over-mcp.md"}], "answer": "We write the Google and GitHub connections ourselves instead of using existing MCP servers because using direct APIs offers full control over error handling, pagination, and rate limits. It also eliminates the dependency on the varying quality and maintenance of community servers and no second auth story is required.", "sources": [{"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "ADR-006-direct-apis-over-mcp", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-006-direct-apis-over-mcp.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "Plan_2", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan_2.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1394, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 18.0, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 2071, "output_tokens": 54, "seconds": 27.7, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 45.9, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q005", "question": "what protections did I have to build before the app was allowed to change files in my vault?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-005-obsidian-read-only-v1.md"}], "answer": "You had to build a snapshot before any modification, an undo path that restores the snapshot, confirmation before modifying files, and tests for the failure cases, among other protections.", "sources": [{"title": "LEARNING", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/LEARNING.md"}, {"title": "ADR-005-obsidian-read-only-v1", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-005-obsidian-read-only-v1.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}, {"title": "ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1800, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 20.1, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 2735, "output_tokens": 35, "seconds": 33.2, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 53.4, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q007", "question": "why do we run the AI tracing tool on my own machine instead of a hosted service?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "no-product-name"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-009-langfuse-for-ai-observability.md"}], "answer": "The decision to use Langfuse, self-hosted, was made to address the observability requirement adopted from Plan_2 \u00a712. The project committed to designing observability in when the first LLM call is made, not retrofitting it. Langfuse self-hosted was chosen because it is open-source, framework-agnostic, and OpenTelemetry-compatible, and it meets the project's requirements for observability and traceability. Additionally, the project will wrap Langfuse with a tracing module that exposes plain types only, to avoid leaking Langfuse types or idioms into AI-layer code.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-009-langfuse-for-ai-observability", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-009-langfuse-for-ai-observability.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "LEARNING", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/LEARNING.md"}, {"title": "Plan_2", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan_2.md"}, {"title": "ADR-007-mnemosyne-is-the-ai-layer", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-007-mnemosyne-is-the-ai-layer.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1837, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 20.6, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 3456, "output_tokens": 119, "seconds": 51.3, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 72.0, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "partial", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q008", "question": "how do we decide when to use a ready-made library versus writing it ourselves?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "conceptual"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first.md"}], "answer": "The decision is to use direct SDK and hand-built components instead of a framework. The reasoning is that the project already has working code for many components, and using a framework would introduce complexity and maintenance burden without providing significant benefits. The decision is based on the ADR-008 principle of adopting a tool when it supplies engineering that would take weeks, and cataloging when the design space is unknown but the code is short.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-008-adopt-first-vs-build-first.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "Personal OS System", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS System.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1770, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 19.9, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 3852, "output_tokens": 85, "seconds": 53.0, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 73.1, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "partial", "grade_note": ""}
{"id": "q009", "question": "why doesn't the AI part just copy all my notes into the database so searching is faster?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "many-related-docs"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-007-mnemosyne-is-the-ai-layer.md"}], "answer": "The AI part does not copy all your notes into the database because ADR-001 explicitly opposes the idea of Obsidian leaving the machine. Tracing, which carries retrieved note text, is designed to avoid sending vault content to a hosted backend.", "sources": [{"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "ADR-007-mnemosyne-is-the-ai-layer", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-007-mnemosyne-is-the-ai-layer.md"}, {"title": "Plan_2", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan_2.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "ADR-009-langfuse-for-ai-observability", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-009-langfuse-for-ai-observability.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1442, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 16.8, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 4970, "output_tokens": 50, "seconds": 62.5, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 79.4, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "correct", "grade_note": ""}
