{"id": "q011", "question": "why not use a simple single-file database for an app only I use?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "no-product-name"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-002-postgres-over-sqlite.md"}], "answer": "The reason why not use a simple single-file database for an app only you use is that atomic writes, change detection, and index staleness become your problem.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-002-postgres-over-sqlite", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-002-postgres-over-sqlite.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "ADR-003-raw-sql-over-orm", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-003-raw-sql-over-orm.md"}, {"title": "ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-001-obsidian-as-canonical-knowledge-store.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1367, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 15.0, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 1921, "output_tokens": 33, "seconds": 22.7, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 37.8, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "partial", "grade_note": "it should be both ADR-001 and ADR-002"}
{"id": "q012", "question": "why not use one of the popular AI frameworks to wire up the retrieval pipeline?", "answerable": true, "tags": ["paraphrased", "no-product-name"], "expected": [{"source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks.md"}], "answer": "Based on the search results, it appears that you are considering using one of the popular AI frameworks to wire up the retrieval pipeline. \n\nHowever, in the `AI engineering track` section of the search results, you have already planned out a step-by-step approach to building the AI layer, with a specific order and milestones. You have also mentioned that building AI-2 (hybrid retrieval) before AI-1 (evals) is the mistake to avoid.\n\nTherefore, it seems that you have already decided to implement the AI layer using a custom approach, rather than relying on a popular AI framework. \n\nSo, to answer your question, why not use one of the popular AI frameworks to wire up the retrieval pipeline? \n\nThe reason is that you have already planned out a custom approach to building the AI layer, with a specific order and milestones. Using a popular AI framework would deviate from this plan and may introduce unexpected complexities or limitations. \n\nYou have also mentioned that you want to keep the system useful even if all AI functionality is disabled, which suggests that you are looking for a more modular and flexible approach to building the AI layer. \n\nTherefore, sticking to your custom approach seems like the best option.", "sources": [{"title": "ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/ADR-010-no-langchain-or-ingestion-frameworks.md"}, {"title": "Plan", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan.md"}, {"title": "backlog", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/backlog.md"}, {"title": "phase-0", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/phase-0.md"}, {"title": "Plan_2", "source": "obsidian", "provider_id": "Personal OS/Plan_2.md"}], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "retrieval_found": true, "calls": [{"prompt_tokens": 1288, "output_tokens": 18, "seconds": 12.4, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": ["get_note"]}, {"prompt_tokens": 4816, "output_tokens": 245, "seconds": 100.1, "load_seconds": 0.0, "tool_calls": []}], "seconds": 112.6, "checks": {"malformed": null, "refused": false}, "grade": "partial", "grade_note": ""}
